This mobile UI for "Nestlé Retailer Direct" follows a classic dashboard pattern. To adapt this into a desktop web application, we need to transition from a vertical, thumb-driven layout to a horizontal, mouse-driven layout that utilizes the extra screen real estate for better visibility.Here is a breakdown of the UI components and how to translate them for the web:1. Global Navigation & HeaderOn a desktop, the bottom navigation bar and top user profile should be consolidated into a Persistent Sidebar or a Fixed Top Navigation Bar.Top Bar: Contains the "Nestlé Retailer Direct" logo (left), a Search bar for products (center), and User Profile/Store Name ("Arunie's Grocery Store") with a logout dropdown (right).Left Sidebar: Navigation links for Home, Orders, Inventory, Promotions, and Account Settings.2. Notification / Alert SystemThe "Low Stock" warning is a high-priority banner.Web Implementation: Place this as a Dashboard Banner at the very top of the main content area.Interaction: Keep the "Restock Now" button, but perhaps add a "Dismiss" or "View All Alerts" option.3. The Dashboard Grid (Main Content)On mobile, these are large buttons. On a desktop, these should be Actionable Widgets or Summary Cards.FeatureMobile VersionDesktop Web RecommendationOne-Tap ReorderSingle ButtonA Quick-Action Widget showing the last 3 orders with a "Reorder" button next to each.Inventory SnapshotSingle ButtonA Mini-Table showing top 5 moving items and current stock levels.My OrdersSingle ButtonA Summary List of "Active Orders" with status trackers (e.g., Shipped, Processing).PromotionsSingle ButtonA Visual Carousel or sidebar highlights of active Nestlé discounts.4. Visual Language & StyleTo maintain brand consistency, the desktop app should use:Color Palette: Deep Navy Blue (#00447C approx.) for primary headers/sidebars, White for the background, and Yellow for alerts.Typography: Clean, sans-serif font (like Lato or Roboto).Cards: Use subtle drop shadows and rounded corners (8px–12px) to keep the "app-like" modern feel.5. Layout Structure (Wireframe Suggestion)Left 20%: Navigation Sidebar.Top 10%: Header with Search and Profile.Center 70%: * Row 1: High-priority Alerts (Low stock).Row 2: 3-column grid of "Quick Stats" (Total Orders, Inventory Value, Pending Tasks).Row 3: Two large panels—Recent Orders (Left) and Inventory Management (Right).Note on Data Redundancy: The mobile screenshot shows "My Orders" and "Promotions" repeated twice. For the web version, ensure these are unique sections to avoid user confusion.